.TH XD\-DESK 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-desk \- Display Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-desk
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-desk
is Display Properties (Control Panel > Display), with Windows 2000's tabs:
.TP
.B Background
The wallpaper and how it is placed.
.TP
.B Screen Saver
The screen saver, its settings and a preview, the Wait, Password protected,
and when to turn the monitors off.
.TP
.B Appearance
The visual style (Classic, Luna, Watercolor or Aero), colour scheme and
font size, with a preview; in Aero, Windows 7's window colours.
.TP
.B Effects
Font smoothing, large icons, the icon theme, and the GTK and Qt styles of
other programs.
.TP
.B Settings
Each monitor's position, resolution, refresh rate, scale and orientation,
or turning it off.
New display settings revert after 15 seconds unless kept.
.PP
Apply and OK write
.IR desktop.ini ,
which the compositor, the shell and the other programs follow at once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.IR n ,
from 0 (Background) to 4 (Settings); the default is 2 (Appearance), as
Windows' desk.cpl.
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
.TQ
.BI \-\-scheme " file"
The visual style and colour scheme of the dialog instead of those in
.IR desktop.ini .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.BR [Appearance] ,
.BR [Desktop] ,
.BR [Wallpaper] ,
.BR [Effects] ,
.B [ScreenSaver]
and
.BR [ScreenSaver.*] .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/monitors.ini
The monitors' settings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xeondesktop/schemes/
The colour schemes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-lock (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
